GLOS shell 1.0. HELP lists its commands.

[[C:\>]]
format c:
FORMAT C: is DISK C: FORMAT
(EXTRA "DISK C: FORMAT" args=2)
(ENDED 0)
[[C:\>]]
format d: /v:new /q /y
FORMAT D: is DISK D: FORMAT /V:new /Y
(EXTRA "DISK D: FORMAT /V:new /Y" args=4)
(ENDED 0)
[[C:\>]]
sys c:
SYS C: is DISK C: BOOT
(EXTRA "DISK C: BOOT" args=2)
(ENDED 0)
[[C:\>]]
sys d: /y
SYS D: is DISK D: BOOT /Y
(EXTRA "DISK D: BOOT /Y" args=3)
(ENDED 0)
[[C:\>]]
fdisk
FDISK's menus are not GLOS's: DISK n NEW, DISK n FORMAT [p] and DISK n INSTALL change the disks.
(EXTRA "DISK" args=0)
(ENDED 0)
[[C:\>]]
fdisk /status
FDISK's menus are not GLOS's: DISK n NEW, DISK n FORMAT [p] and DISK n INSTALL change the disks.
(EXTRA "DISK" args=0)
(ENDED 0)
[[C:\>]]
format
<<Required parameter missing
>>[[C:\>]]
echo %errorlevel%
1
[[C:\>]]
format a:
<<FORMAT: GLOS's DISK formats hard disks' partitions, not floppies
>>[[C:\>]]
format c: /s
<<FORMAT /S: SYS d: after it (DISK's BOOT)
>>[[C:\>]]
format c: /f:1440
<<Invalid switch - /f:1440
>>[[C:\>]]
sys b:
<<SYS: GLOS's DISK writes hard disks' boot records, not floppies'
>>[[C:\>]]
fdisk 1 2
<<FDISK's menus are not GLOS's: DISK lists the disks, DISK n NEW, DISK n FORMAT [p] and DISK n INSTALL change them
>>[[C:\>]]
format c: d:
<<Invalid parameter - d:
>>[[C:\>]]
exit
(QUIT 0)
[[C:\>]]

